WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.440
The One Piece manga just CONFIRMED the shocking
end of the conflict on Pirate Island, where

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:09.480
Monkey D. Garp was defeated and most likely
captured by the Blackbeard Pirates.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.980
Which is absolutely game changing for the
story because this will surely lead to some

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.980
world altering events that could involve the
Marines, Cross Guild, the Straw hats, and

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.150
even the secret ruler of the world, Imu.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.320
And that’s not the only thing that happened
in this chapter because Koby also revealed

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:31.210
what could be the future justice system of
the marines, plus he demonstrated his incredible

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.110
new strength for the very first time.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:37.550
To top it off, we finally seem to be headed
back to Egghead Island in the very near future

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.330
where we will finally see the events that
will shock the world.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:46.800
But whatever twists are to come during Egghead,
it is going to be hard to live up to the insanity

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.120
of the Hero of the Marines being defeated.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:55.120
Because back in chapter 1071 when Garp first
announced he was going to save Koby, I don’t

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.280
think ANYONE seriously thought that he would
lose and be captured like this.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:05.710
Because in this chapter Garp nearly takes
out the island man Pizzaro all by himself

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:11.400
and shows off his impressive speed that even
surprises the former admiral Kuzan, but he

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.320
eventually gets surrounded by the Blackbeard
pirates.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.509
Koby and the others have made it safely to
the escaping ship, which we’ll discuss more

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:22.800
in just a moment, and even though Koby wants
to return to help Garp, he is already being

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:43.299
frozen by Kuzan, just like what happened to
Saul back in chapter 397.

00:01:43.299 --> 00:02:51.709
Now 

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:56.930
before we go any further into what this means
for Garp’s future let’s talk about what

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.849
this means for Kuzan.

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:04.480
And even though at this point you might say
it is major copium, I’m still not convinced

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:09.200
Kuzan is evil because maybe the ice man knew
that Garp was going to die from his stab wound

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:14.860
in the last chapter, so freezing him was a
way to keep him alive while his body heals,

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.440
kinda like going into cryofreeze.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.840
Plus I’m sure the rest of the Blackbeard
pirates would have kept stabbing and shooting

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:26.050
Garp until they knew he was dead, but if he
is frozen then it makes sense that they stopped.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:32.010
And&nbsp; It is also a convenient way to keep
Garp trapped, although we’ve seen characters

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:35.890
break out of ice before.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:40.620
Before we get back to Garp’s future, there
is one other mind-blowing point I want to

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.319
make about what all this means for Kuzan.

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:47.940
Because if you look at the title of this chapter,
it is called “Last Lesson”.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:53.540
So I’m wondering if this scene where Garp
sacrifices himself to save Koby is actually

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.930
the so-called last lesson that Garp is trying
to teach Kuzan.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:02.590
Because if Garp is willing to give up his
life to protect the person that he most believes

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:07.810
in, then maybe Kuzan is being set up to do
the very same thing in the future.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.620
And if we are thinking along these lines,
then the person that makes the most sense

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:16.290
for him to sacrifice himself for would definitely
be Nico Robin.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:20.509
Because as we pointed out in the last chapter,
Kuzan let her live after the destruction of

00:04:20.509 --> 00:04:25.759
Ohara, and ever since he has been waiting
to see what kind of person she will become.

00:04:25.759 --> 00:04:32.210
So could we see him give up his life to save
Robin during the fight between Blackbeard’s

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.979
crew and the Straw Hats?

00:04:34.979 --> 00:04:40.199
But whatever Kuzan’s future role is, I think
it is fair to say that we all thought Garp’s

00:04:40.199 --> 00:04:45.320
role would be a whole lot different than we
see at the end of this chapter.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:53.009
I mean he is the Hero of the Marines and many
consider him the strongest marine.

00:04:53.009 --> 00:04:59.509
Plus he is Luffy’s grandpa which means he
should have some major role in the story.

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:04.780
Which could still turn out to be the case
just not in the way we were expecting.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:09.509
And in the last chapter review, we speculated
on exactly what could happen in the future

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:11.780
if Garp was indeed captured.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.949
To sum it up, there are essentially three
options for what the Blackbeard pirates could

00:05:15.949 --> 00:05:16.949
do with Garp.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:22.410
First, they could straight up kill him, but
since Kuzan took the trouble to freeze him,

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:32.330
that doesn’t seem likely at this point.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:36.690
The second option was for the Blackbeard pirates
to hand Garp over to Cross Guild to set up

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:42.610
a sort of Reverse Marineford, where the pirates
are executing a marine.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:47.130
And the third option was for Blackbeard to
try to ransom Garp to the World Government

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:51.509
in exchange for being recognized as an official
kingdom.

00:05:51.509 --> 00:05:57.270
And at this point, I don’t think any of
those options have changed, but since it is

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:02.880
now confirmed that Garp is defeated, let’s
dive a bit deeper into how each of these options

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.530
could play out and why they make sense for
the story.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:12.470
As I already said, the option I still think
is most unlikely is Garp straight up dying

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.470
right now.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:17.430
I mean the only purpose that would serve is
to inspire Luffy to get revenge and for Koby

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.650
to inherit Garp’s will of being a great,
honest marine.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:27.319
Which just doesn't seem epic enough for a
character like Garp at this point

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:32.360
But that is nowhere near as exciting as if
Garp gets turned over to Cross Guild for an

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:33.360
execution.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:38.460
And with a 3 Billion berry bounty, I kinda
wonder how the leaders of Cross Guild would

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:43.830
even pay that amount, but let’s assume they
do get their hands on Garp, then we could

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:48.770
be in for a global broadcast execution on
the scale of Marineford.

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:53.919
And I’m sure Garp’s marine friends would
come to save him unless they were ordered

00:06:53.919 --> 00:06:54.919
not to.

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:58.030
Which might cause even more marines to resign
if that were to happen.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:01.789
I’d also expect Luffy to come save his Grandpa.

00:07:01.789 --> 00:07:07.830
Shanks could show up as well, which could
actually have disastrous consequences, which

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.150
we’ll discuss more in just a moment.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:14.990
Honestly though, I don’t think Oda would
have another execution style epic war just

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:20.050
for the sake of it, so let’s analyze some
of the reasons Marineford was so impactful

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:21.050
on the story.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:26.010
First, before the war even started the darkness
fruit user snuck into Impel Down and recruited

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.990
some powerful prisoners onto his crew.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:33.960
So if we are having another kind of war like
Marineford, I wonder if Blackbeard would try

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:37.520
to do something similar and steal another
prisoner out of Impel Down.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:42.720
And if you are wondering who that might be,
well look no further than this pink guy.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.580
No, wait, not that one.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:45.580
This one.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:50.169
That’s right, you may have forgotten that
Doflamingo is still in jail, but he is AND

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:55.669
more importantly he knows some of the world
government's deepest secrets knows, in particular

00:07:55.669 --> 00:08:01.539
the national treasure of Mary Geoise, which
still hasn't been confirmed exactly what this

00:08:01.539 --> 00:08:02.539
is.

00:08:02.539 --> 00:08:07.040
And that is exactly the type of information
that I am sure Blackbeard would love to get

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.180
his hands on.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:12.240
Which brings us to the next important aspect
of Marineford, which was that the person being

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.120
executed had someone very special to them
try to rescue them.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:20.400
And that special person - which was Whitebeard
- ended up dying.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:25.479
But what’s important about the former Yonko’s
death was that it was all part of Blackbeard’s

00:08:25.479 --> 00:08:28.120
plot to steal a second devil fruit.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:34.180
So if we have a second Marineford style war,
even if it was a smaller scale, this could

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:40.779
be another opportunity for Blackbeard to swoop
in and steal another super powerful devil

00:08:40.779 --> 00:08:42.209
fruit.

00:08:42.209 --> 00:08:47.220
Maybe Luffy's, Sengoku's Buddha Fruit, or
one of the admirals' powers might make sense.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:51.760
Or if it wasn’t a devil fruit that Blackbeard
is after, maybe he could be coming to steal

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.630
Poneglyph copies during the chaos of the fighting.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:59.600
And if we focus on Whitebeard dying, the final
thing I could see possibly happening in this

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:04.660
scenario is Blackbeard taking advantage of
the fighting to finally have his long-awaited

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.079
showdown with Shanks.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:11.250
Because at Marineford, Shanks offered to fight
Blackbeard, but the darkness fruit user said

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:13.770
that this wasn’t the time for them to fight.

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:20.000
So what better opportunity to finally have
this epic clash than at a Reverse Marineford?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:25.370
And if they fight, I would certainly be sweating
that Shanks could die in this scenario.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:31.089
Because I mean we all know Blackbeard is one
of Luffy’s end game villains, so he probably

00:09:31.089 --> 00:09:35.180
won’t be defeated by anyone other than Luffy.

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:42.899
But that’s not even the most insane character
that Blackbeard might defeat out of this whole

00:09:42.899 --> 00:09:46.750
situation, so make sure to subscribe to the
channel for more One Piece content like this.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:51.510
And I say that because if Blackbeard doesn’t
hand Garp over to Cross Guild then the other

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:55.740
likely option is that he tries to ransom the
Hero of the Marines in exchange for Pirate

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:59.610
Island being officially recognized as part
of the world government.

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:04.900
Of course that would make Blackbeard king,
which if I'm being honest it is entirely possible

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:09.250
the world government would simply refuse and
not give Blackbeard what he wants.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:14.140
But let’s assume for a minute that they
do agree and Blackbeard becomes an official

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:16.240
king of the world government.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:21.880
And I’m warning you right now, strap on
your seatbelts because if this happens could

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:26.610
change everything that we know about the final
war at the end of the story.

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:31.209
To set this up, let’s head back to chapter
907, where we are first introduced to the

00:10:31.209 --> 00:10:32.860
Empty Throne in Mary Geoise.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:37.500
Here we can see that this annoying guy right
here is making his oath as the new king of

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.600
the Goa Kingdom.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:43.639
To do this he is supposed to place a blade
before the empty throne and swear to not try

00:10:43.639 --> 00:10:46.100
to seek control over other kingdoms.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:52.430
Now, no one really cares about Stelly, but
this is important to think about if we are

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:56.800
considering Blackbeard could become an official
king of the world government.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:01.170
Because it is reasonable to assume that Blackbeard
would also be required to come in and make

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:03.390
this oath before the empty throne.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:08.350
Of course, Blackbeard would probably never
make that promise, but the key point is that

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.790
Blackbeard would supposedly have access to
Mary Geoise.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:17.870
And man my mind just goes crazy when thinking
about Blackbeard strolling around the Holy

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:18.870
Land.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:23.310
Because who is to say that Blackbeard doesn’t
already know about some of the secrets hidden

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.339
up here on top of the Red Line.

00:11:25.339 --> 00:11:28.080
Could he know about Imu?

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:33.690
Or is there some other secret like a devil
fruit tree that he might be interested in?

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:37.570
There are so many possibilities in this scenario!

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:45.920
But if all of this does happen and Blackbeard
finds himself in the castle, then I could

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:49.740
see something happening that could completely
change the entire story.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:55.519
Because in chapter 1085 we were first shown
the Gorosei and Imu’s powers.

00:11:55.519 --> 00:12:01.070
And while these powers were kept in silhouette,
many people have also speculated that Imu

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:05.520
really does have some sort of powers relating
to darkness, shadow, or nightmares.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:11.390
So I am super curious how these powers would
fare against Blackbeard’s darkness fruit

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:12.870
powers.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.860
Could Blackbeard’s darkness negate Imu’s
abilities?

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:21.019
And if they fight then the outcome could shake
the entire world.

00:12:21.019 --> 00:12:27.700
I mean can you imagine if Blackbeard somehow
took out Imu and the Gorosei?

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:33.570
Which might sound crazy, but just think about
it for a moment.

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:37.680
One thing that has always been strange to
me about end game One Piece is that there

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:41.380
are basically two final boss type characters.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:46.389
Blackbeard and Imu.

00:12:46.389 --> 00:12:50.480
And if we assume that Luffy is supposed to
fight Blackbeard for the One Piece, then does

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:53.230
he go and fight Imu after that?

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:56.660
Or does Imu come to Laugh Tale?

00:12:56.660 --> 00:13:04.980
It honestly seems a bit weird since finding
the one piece has always seemed like the climax

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:05.980
of the story.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:11.930
So wouldn’t it make sense if these two final
bosses fought each other and only one emerged

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:14.139
as the final super villain?

00:13:14.139 --> 00:13:17.800
Wow, we are way deep into theory territory
here.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:22.480
And you might think I am crazy for speculating
all of this based on the simple fact of Garp

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.600
being captured.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:30.260
But we've already seen how much a single event
can change the world.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:37.540
Just look back at Ace being captured and all
of the mind-blogging madness that resulted

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:38.540
in.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:44.750
But there are a few other super interesting
points from the chapter that hint at endgame

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.550
outcomes for One Piece.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:53.120
The first is that we see Koby finally unleash
an impressive attack, which is called Honesty

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.060
Impact.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:14:01.420
With his a haki covered fist that very much
resembles Garp’s devastatingly powerful

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:08.040
Galaxy Impact that we just saw in chapter
1080, he completely destroys the giant hand

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:11.180
that is about to crush the escaping marine
vessel.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:16.670
Koby has learned a thing or two from Garp,
but what I am most interested in is the “Honesty”

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:21.079
part of the attack name because I think this
could be important foreshadowing for the type

00:14:21.079 --> 00:14:27.670
of Justice that Koby will embrace when he
eventually becomes an admiral in the marines.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:32.750
I mean it goes along with his character, and
it is a stark contrast to the corruption that

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:36.540
exists in the current world government and
marines.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:41.829
The world government is actually incredibly
dishonest in many situations, especially when

00:14:41.829 --> 00:14:46.910
they tried to cover up the horrible events
in Alabasta and Dressrosa.

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:52.680
So I’m definitely looking forward to some
change in philosophy that Koby will likely

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.519
bring in the future.

00:14:54.519 --> 00:15:00.209
Plus we finally got to see more of why exactly
Garp believes so much in Koby, because we

00:15:00.209 --> 00:15:04.620
get to see many of their interactions during
Koby’s time training and see just how hard

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:07.370
he hard to work to become as strong as he
has.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:11.889
But that’s the only impressive thing he
does because we also get to see exactly how

00:15:11.889 --> 00:15:14.700
Koby ended up captured by Blackbeard.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:20.149
In chapter 1059 we saw the start of this conflict
on Amazon Lily, where Blackbeard attacked

00:15:20.149 --> 00:15:23.850
with the hope of taking the pirate Empress
Boa Hancock’s devil fruit.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:28.880
And while the Yonko was stopped by a combination
of Koby, the Seraphim, and Silver’s Rayleigh,

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:34.500
it turns out that Blackbeard was going to
take hundreds of marines with his as prisoner.

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:40.670
That is until Koby traded himself for all
of those marines, which is how he ended up

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:42.149
captured.

00:15:42.149 --> 00:15:46.770
And if that’s not what you call being a
“hero” than I don’t know what is, so

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:51.360
it makes even more sense now why Garp has
so much faith in Koby.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:56.390
Shifting back to the end of the chapter, we
got a narrator box which explained that tomorrow’s

00:15:56.390 --> 00:16:02.040
newspaper has information that Koby was safe,
Garp disappeared on Pirate Island, and apparently

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:06.230
that Luffy is going to claim Egghead Island
as his own territory.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:12.160
Now we have to keep in mind that this is the
newspaper which usually exaggerates things,

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:16.120
but regardless it seems we finally shift back
to Egghead Island.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:20.600
We even get to see that the ships carrying
Saint Saturn and Admiral Kizaru are finally

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.330
pulling up to the island.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:27.060
So After nine whole chapters away, we are
finally going to return for the conclusion

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:30.920
of this arc that we were literally told will
shock the world.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:37.130
And wow I am so excited to see the straw hats
again, in particular their inevitable encounter

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:39.560
with Saint Saturn.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:46.670
After seeing a bit of what his powers can
do in chapter 1085 I simply cannot wait to

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:49.190
see him and Admiral Kizaru in action against
Luffy.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:52.790
However, we have to remember that they are
not the only ones here.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:57.170
Because we also know that someone from Blackbeard’s
crew is here as well, which brings us back

00:16:57.170 --> 00:17:00.430
to the question of what they could also be
doing here.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:05.100
And one idea that I saw on Twitter from 3SkullJoe
was that Blackbeard could be bringing Big

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:09.579
Mom’s daughter, Pudding, to try and use
her devil fruit powers to get some top secret

00:17:09.579 --> 00:17:13.980
information out of Vegapunk.

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:19.049
In case you forgot, Pudding has the memory
devil fruit, which lets her see and manipulate

00:17:19.049 --> 00:17:20.559
a person’s memories.

00:17:20.559 --> 00:17:26.030
So if Pudding is forced to use her powers
on the genius scientist, I wonder what information

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:27.480
he could be after.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:30.600
Plans for some incredibly powerful technology?

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:34.260
Secrets about the Void Century or how to read
the poneglyphs?

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:41.740
And even if this isn’t the case, Blackbeard
might be able to use Pudding on the newly

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:45.610
captured Garp to retrieve some memories from
the Hero of the Marines.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:49.340
And what memories might Blackbeard be after
in this case?

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:55.049
Well, how about information about the person
who inspired Blackbeard, Rocks D. Xebec?

00:17:55.049 --> 00:18:00.480
After all, Garp was the one who defeated Rocks
with the help of Roger, so he is sure to know

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:04.370
information about the infamous pirate from
forty years ago.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:10.370
And hold on, if this were to happen then does
that mean we could actually get a real flashback

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:12.620
to the events of God Valley?

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:18.600
If I’m being honest, I have been dying to
see the legendary clash between Roger, Garp,

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:24.860
and Rocks, which I bet would undoubtedly be
one of the most hyped up moments in the entire

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:25.860
story.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:29.880
And if all of this has got you wanting a pure
injection of the most badass moments in the

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:34.780
entire story, then you can check out my ranking
of the most exciting moments in one piece

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:35.780
right here.

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:38.410
Shanks for watching and I’ll see you in
the next one.

